lookups-note = MusicBrainz for what a release and an artist are, the Cover Art Archive for a cover, Wikimedia Commons for a portrait, LRCLIB and Better Lyrics for lyrics. Nothing sent identifies you unless a contact is given below.
mirror-note = MusicBrainz's own export, a 7.5 GB download read into a copy of about 10 GB kept here, compressed and indexed; the build wants some 50 GB of room for about an hour. A lookup is answered from it in milliseconds, before the network, and a synced device without a copy asks this one.
mirror-absent = No copy is held yet. Building one fetches the export and reads it, which takes a while; lookups go on as before meanwhile.
metered-note = A connection NetworkManager reports as metered, a phone's hotspot or a capped plan, is the one these switches are about; one it cannot tell is taken as not metered. A song played in place is neither skipped nor held.
waiting-on-the-meter = The connection is metered: downloads wait for one that is not, and go on by themselves when it changes.
next-start-note = Turned on for the next start; nothing is reached until then.
key-note = Used from the next start by the lookup, which names by ear what nothing else could, and by the Analysis pane. Leave it empty to recognise nothing.
token-note = Used from the next start by Listen, which asks AudD beside Shazam. Leave it empty to ask Shazam alone.
submitting-note = Followed as soon as it is given: every play counted from then on is sent to ListenBrainz within a minute. Leave it empty to send nothing.
earlier-plays-note = Plays counted before the token was given are kept here and not sent unless asked: every one of them goes to ListenBrainz, a hundred at a time.
earlier-plays-asked = The earlier plays are on their way, a hundred a minute, oldest first.
by-sound-note = A lookup that finds no name, recording id or ISRC to ask with, and no AcoustID answer, sends Shazam the peaks of twelve seconds of the track and asks MusicBrainz for what it names. The Analysis pane recognises the same way.
listening-note = Listen names a song playing on the desktop or into a microphone, whether or not the library holds it. A microphone named in the Listen sheet is kept here too.
the-desktop = The desktop
a-microphone = A microphone
listen-names-what-this-machine-is = Listen names what this machine is playing — a video, a stream, another player — by recording the desktop's own output.
listen-names-what-is-playing-in = Listen names what is playing in the room, heard through the microphone chosen below.
other = Other
quickest-to-answer-enough-for-a = Quickest to answer; enough for a clear recording of a well-known song.
enough-for-most-songs-even-over = Enough for most songs, even over a little noise.
the-best-chance-with-a-noisy = The best chance with a noisy room, a quiet passage or a rarer song.
a-length-of-your-own-set = A length of your own, set in the settings file.
contact-note = Sent in the User-Agent to MusicBrainz, the Cover Art Archive, ListenBrainz and Wikimedia, which ask who is asking, from the next request on. Leave it empty to send nothing.
reach-the-network = Reach the network
off-the-library-is-what-the = Off, the library is what the files say
keep-a-copy-of-musicbrainz-here = Keep a copy of MusicBrainz here
off-musicbrainz-is-asked-over-the = Off, MusicBrainz is asked over the network or of a synced device
build-it-again = Build it again
build-it-now = Build it now
remove-the-copy = Remove the copy
ask-as-soon-as-a-scan = Ask as soon as a scan ends
off-the-reference-is-asked-only = Off, the reference is asked only when Enrich is pressed
look-things-up-on-a-metered = Look things up on a metered connection
off-the-reference-is-not-asked = Off, the reference is not asked while the connection is metered
hold-downloads-while-the-connection-is = Hold downloads while the connection is metered
off-a-providers-downloads-go-on = Off, a provider's downloads go on whatever the connection
study-every-track-as-a-lookup = Study every track as a lookup runs
off-a-track-is-decoded-only = Off, a track is decoded only to be heard or named
name-a-track-nothing-else-can = Name a track nothing else can by how it sounds
off-no-tracks-sound-is-sent = Off, no track's sound is sent to Shazam
fetch-lyrics-for-every-track-as = Fetch lyrics for every track as a lookup runs
off-words-are-asked-for-only = Off, words are asked for only as a track plays
choose-a-lyric-sheet-in-the = Choose a lyric sheet in the language the system is set to
off-of-sheets-in-several-languages = Off, of sheets in several languages the first by name is read
user-token = User token
press-again-to-send-every-earlier = Press again to send every earlier play
send-earlier-plays = Send earlier plays
listen-to = Listen to
for = For
mirror-building-so-far = Building: { $doing }, { $read } of { $of } GB.
mirror-building = Building: { $doing }.
mirror-held = The export of { $dump } is held, { $held } GB on disc.
mirror-held-and-followed = The export of { $dump } is held, { $held } GB on disc, and MusicBrainz's changes were last followed { $ago }.
replication-note = A MetaBrainz access token, free from metabrainz.org for use that is not commercial, lets the copy follow MusicBrainz's hourly changes, so it is never more than an hour behind. The next build keeps the export's tables beside the copy for it, some 30 GB more. Leave it empty to refresh the copy only from each new export.
mirror-failed = The last build failed: { $why }.
